 "bloques": [
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "And then: -",
   "texto": [
    "Para encadenar acciones relacionadas, se añade **-고** a la raíz del primer verbo: 보다 → **보고**, 먹다 → **먹고**. En una secuencia sencilla con el mismo sujeto, suele bastar con marcar el pasado en el último verbo: 바다를 **보고** 사진을 찍었어요 = vi el mar e hice fotos.",
    "It is not an absolute rule: the past may also appear before - namely when the clauses are presented as separate facts or their temporal relationship is emphasized."
   ]
  },
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "That's why, but, by the way,",
   "texto": [
    "**그래서** = that's why. **그래서** - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -",
    "**하지만** = but.",
    "**그런데** = but, and also «by the way.», to change the subject.",
    "**그리고** = and, in addition."
   ]
  },
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "To count a trip",
   "texto": [
    "**도착했어요** = arrived. **탔어요** = I took (a transport). **걸었어요** = walked. **구경했어요** = I visited, I was watching.",
    "**어땠어요?** = how was it? It's the past of the city. **좋았어요** = was fine.",
    "**다시** = again."
   ]
  },
